      "message": "maybe, in another tasks we can switch away from \"counting generations\", add one and add a fixme:\n- netconf\u0027s NetconfNodeHandler (apps/netconf-topology/.../spi/NetconfNodeHandler.java) is a genuinely better idiom, though still not a formal FSM: instead of a generation counter, the \"current attempt\" is an object (Task — ConnectingTask/SleepingTask) held in a @GuardedBy(\"this\") Task currentTask field, and a completing callback checks task.equals(currentTask) — identity comparison instead of counter comparison. Idempotent close comes for free from yangtools\u0027 AbstractRegistration base class rather than being hand-rolled per class (which is exactly the closed boolean gnmi had to add manually to SessionProviderImpl and GnmiConnectionStatusListener in this PR). Worth a look as a refactor direction if this pattern needs to be hardened further.",
